<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mulay Hasan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1526">1526</a>–<a href="/years/1543">1543</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Muley Hassan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mulay Hasan was a Hafsid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> who came to the throne in 1526. Driven out by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hayreddin-barbarossa">Hayreddin Barbarossa</a> in 1534, he was restored the following year by the Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, whose expedition captured Tunis, and ruled as a Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> with a Spanish garrison at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-goulette">La Goulette</a>. In 1542–1543 he was deposed and blinded by his son Ahmad, and he died in exile.</p></div>
